 Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.028","title":["Mapping to Open-Source Packages"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.028","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.004","title":["Agent Architectures and Hierarchical Control"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.004","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.5220\/0013249800003890","title":["Advancing Polycystic Ovary Syndrome Detection with Artificial Intelligence Techniques"],"author":[{"given":"Abir","family":"Gorrab","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"RIADI Laboratory, National School of Computer Science, University of Manouba, Tunisia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Nourh\u00e8ne","family":"Ben Rabah","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Centre de Recherche en Informatique, Universit\u00e9 Paris1 Panth\u00e9on-Sorbonne, France"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Isuri","family":"Kariyawasam","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Centre de Recherche en Informatique, Universit\u00e9 Paris1 Panth\u00e9on-Sorbonne, France"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"B\u00e9n\u00e9dicte","family":"Le Grand","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Centre de Recherche en Informatique, Universit\u00e9 Paris1 Panth\u00e9on-Sorbonne, France"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5220\/0013249800003890","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["Proceedings of the 17th International Conference on Agents and Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.5220\/0012270700003636","title":["Artificial Intelligence for Visualization, Processing and Predict of Temperature and Fluid Flow Modeling"],"author":[{"given":"Vishal","family":"Nandigana","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Fluid Systems Laboratory (FSL), Department of Mechanical Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Madras, Chennai 600036, Tamil Nadu, India, --- Select a Country ---"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5220\/0012270700003636","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["Proceedings of the 16th International Conference on Agents and Artificial Intelligence"]},{"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Fully revised and updated, this third edition includes three new chapters on neural networks and deep learning including generative AI, causality, and the social, ethical and regulatory impacts of artificial intelligence. All parts have been updated with the methods that have been proven to work. The book's novel agent design space provides a coherent framework for learning, reasoning and decision making. Numerous realistic applications and examples facilitate student understanding. Every concept or algorithm is presented in pseudocode and open source AIPython code, enabling students to experiment with and build on the implementations. Five larger case studies are developed throughout the book and connect the design approaches to the applications. Each chapter now has a social impact section, enabling students to understand the impact of the various techniques as they learn them. An invaluable teaching package for undergraduate and graduate AI courses, this comprehensive textbook is accompanied by lecture slides, solutions, and code.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227","title":["Artificial Intelligence"],"author":[{"given":"David L.","family":"Poole","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Alan K.","family":"Mackworth","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2023,8,14]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227"},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.016","title":["Planning and Acting with Uncertainty"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.016","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.24963\/ijcai.2024\/2","title":["AriGraph: Learning Knowledge Graph World Models with Episodic Memory for LLM Agents"],"author":[{"given":"Petr","family":"Anokhin","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"AIRI, Moscow, Russia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Nikita","family":"Semenov","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Skoltech, Moscow, Russia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Artyom","family":"Sorokin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"AIRI, Moscow, Russia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Dmitry","family":"Evseev","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Skoltech, Moscow, Russia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Andrey","family":"Kravchenko","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Oxford, UK"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mikhail","family":"Burtsev","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"London Institute for Mathematical Sciences, London, UK"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Evgeny","family":"Burnaev","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Skoltech, Moscow, Russia"},{"name":"AIRI, Moscow, Russia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.24963\/ijcai.2024\/2","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,8]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,8]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Advancements in the capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs) have created a promising foundation for developing autonomous agents. With the right tools, these agents could learn to solve tasks in new environments by accumulating and updating their knowledge. Current LLM-based agents process past experiences using a full history of observations, summarization, retrieval augmentation. However, these unstructured memory representations do not facilitate the reasoning and planning essential for complex decision-making. In our study, we introduce AriGraph, a novel method wherein the agent constructs and updates a memory graph that integrates semantic and episodic memories while exploring the environment. We demonstrate that our Ariadne LLM agent, consisting of the proposed memory architecture augmented with planning and decision-making, effectively handles complex tasks within interactive text game environments difficult even for human players. Results show that our approach markedly outperforms other established memory methods and strong RL baselines in a range of problems of varying complexity. Additionally, AriGraph demonstrates competitive performance compared to dedicated knowledge graph-based methods in static multi-hop question-answering.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Proceedings of the Thirty-ThirdInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/icdsaai65575.2025.11011611","title":["Diagnosis of Hemorrhage in Wireless CapsuleEndoscopy Images using a Hybrid Convolutional Neural Network -Long Short Term Memory (CNN \u2013LSTM) Model"],"author":[{"given":"Jeeva","family":"S","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"SRM Madurai College for Engineering and Technology,Madurai"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Anand","family":"S","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Mepco Schlenk Engineering College,Sivakasi"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icdsaai65575.2025.11011611","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,28]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,28]]},"container-title":["2025 International Conference on Data Science, Agents &amp;amp; Artificial Intelligence (ICDSAAI)"]},{"DOI":"10.1142\/9789819815678_0005","title":["PUTTING AI AGENTS TO THE TEST"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1142\/9789819815678_0005","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,7]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,29]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,29]]},"container-title":["Agentic Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1142\/9789819815678_0015","title":["SOCIETY IN THE AGE OF AGENTS"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1142\/9789819815678_0015","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,7]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,29]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,29]]},"container-title":["Agentic Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.4337\/9781803928562.00020","title":["Artificial intelligence and social memory: towards the cyborgian remembrance of an advancing mnemo-technic"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-9572-5922","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Samuel","family":"Merrill","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.4337\/9781803928562.00020","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,11,14]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,11,14]]},"container-title":["Handbook of Critical Studies of Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1088\/978-0-7503-6169-9","title":["Resistive Switching Systems for In-Memory Computation and Artificial Intelligence"],"author":[{"given":"Shaibal","family":"Mukherjee","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Technology Indore","place":["India"]},{"name":"QuanTechL2M Innovations Pvt. Ltd.","place":["India"]}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1088\/978-0-7503-6169-9","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,1]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,1]]}},{"DOI":"10.1080\/08839514.2022.2164401